1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,490
Three in the morning.

2
00:00:02,140 --> 00:00:04,010
Your Hyperliquid position is minutes

3
00:00:03,860 --> 00:00:05,030
from liquidation,

4
00:00:04,880 --> 00:00:06,070
and you're asleep.

5
00:00:07,220 --> 00:00:09,330
It happens to traders every day.

6
00:00:09,900 --> 00:00:11,490
In one October cascade,

7
00:00:11,900 --> 00:00:13,840
over seven point four billion dollars

8
00:00:13,640 --> 00:00:16,830
of Hyperliquid positions were wiped out.

9
00:00:18,360 --> 00:00:18,990
Lifeline,

10
00:00:19,260 --> 00:00:20,150
built on NEAR,

11
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:21,150
stops that.

12
00:00:21,700 --> 00:00:24,030
It watches your account every five seconds,

13
00:00:23,880 --> 00:00:25,950
and tops up your margin from

14
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:27,510
a reserve you fund from any

15
00:00:27,360 --> 00:00:28,930
chain through NEAR Intents.

16
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:32,550
NEAR Intents swaps your funds from

17
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:34,950
any chain into USDC on NEAR,

18
00:00:34,800 --> 00:00:36,750
and you deposit it into the

19
00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:37,450
Lifeline vault.

20
00:00:38,960 --> 00:00:40,250
Then set your rules:

21
00:00:40,640 --> 00:00:41,690
when to warn you,

22
00:00:41,740 --> 00:00:42,630
when to rescue,

23
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:43,870
and how much.

24
00:00:45,280 --> 00:00:46,890
Your policy lives in the vault

25
00:00:46,740 --> 00:00:47,390
on NEAR,

26
00:00:47,240 --> 00:00:49,230
so only you can change it,

27
00:00:49,080 --> 00:00:50,270
from your own wallet.

28
00:00:51,340 --> 00:00:53,230
The keeper reads your health every

29
00:00:53,080 --> 00:00:54,030
five seconds.

30
00:00:54,380 --> 00:00:55,210
At one,

31
00:00:55,420 --> 00:00:56,330
you're liquidated.

32
00:00:57,700 --> 00:00:58,690
Below your trigger,

33
00:00:58,960 --> 00:01:01,050
it gets a signed quote from 1Click,

34
00:01:00,900 --> 00:01:02,850
and the vault pays it straight

35
00:01:02,700 --> 00:01:04,410
into your Hyperliquid margin.

36
00:01:05,880 --> 00:01:06,790
On testnet,

37
00:01:06,940 --> 00:01:09,190
that money reached Hyperliquid in under

38
00:01:09,040 --> 00:01:10,270
fifteen seconds.

39
00:01:11,560 --> 00:01:13,030
You wake up to a message

40
00:01:12,880 --> 00:01:14,010
explaining it.

41
00:01:14,240 --> 00:01:16,070
Every step is on a public ledger.

42
00:01:17,240 --> 00:01:19,710
This test account has thirty-four real

43
00:01:19,560 --> 00:01:21,270
rescues on NEAR testnet,

44
00:01:21,120 --> 00:01:23,310
and each one is a transaction

45
00:01:23,160 --> 00:01:24,150
you can open.

46
00:01:25,340 --> 00:01:27,090
A bot that moves money is

47
00:01:26,940 --> 00:01:27,570
a target.

48
00:01:27,860 --> 00:01:29,970
So we assume it gets hacked.

49
00:01:31,360 --> 00:01:32,590
On the attack page,

50
00:01:32,960 --> 00:01:34,630
anyone can play a hacked keeper

51
00:01:34,480 --> 00:01:35,690
holding the real key.

52
00:01:36,180 --> 00:01:37,430
It tries to pay itself.

53
00:01:39,020 --> 00:01:40,010
The vault refuses,

54
00:01:40,340 --> 00:01:40,930
on chain.

55
00:01:41,780 --> 00:01:43,350
The key can only call rescue,

56
00:01:43,200 --> 00:01:45,570
and the vault checks every quote itself.

57
00:01:47,020 --> 00:01:48,290
Edit a signed quote.

58
00:01:48,700 --> 00:01:50,110
Take more than the cap.

59
00:01:50,540 --> 00:01:51,830
Replay an old one.

60
00:01:51,680 --> 00:01:53,050
Seven tricks,

61
00:01:53,500 --> 00:01:54,530
seven refusals.

62
00:01:56,040 --> 00:01:56,990
Don't trust us:

63
00:01:57,300 --> 00:01:59,350
the verify page checks every claim

64
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:00,050
in your browser,

65
00:02:00,500 --> 00:02:02,910
even each AI explanation's signature.

66
00:02:04,240 --> 00:02:06,630
Each AI explanation is signed inside

67
00:02:06,480 --> 00:02:07,730
a verified enclave,

68
00:02:07,580 --> 00:02:09,670
and your browser checks it against

69
00:02:09,520 --> 00:02:11,490
a fresh hardware report from Intel.

70
00:02:13,480 --> 00:02:16,050
Centralised exchanges sell auto top-up,

71
00:02:15,900 --> 00:02:18,030
but only inside their own walls,

72
00:02:17,880 --> 00:02:20,150
and only for isolated margin.

73
00:02:20,660 --> 00:02:22,550
Lifeline works across chains,

74
00:02:22,840 --> 00:02:24,010
from your own wallet,

75
00:02:23,860 --> 00:02:25,670
and not even our own keeper

76
00:02:25,520 --> 00:02:26,650
can take the money.

77
00:02:28,400 --> 00:02:29,470
And it needs NEAR.

78
00:02:30,100 --> 00:02:32,170
Intents move the money from any

79
00:02:32,020 --> 00:02:33,310
chain in one step.

80
00:02:33,660 --> 00:02:35,630
A function-call key lets the keeper

81
00:02:35,480 --> 00:02:37,330
call rescue and nothing else.

82
00:02:37,860 --> 00:02:39,630
The vault checks 1Click's signature

83
00:02:39,480 --> 00:02:40,330
on chain.

84
00:02:40,860 --> 00:02:43,170
And NEAR AI explains every rescue

85
00:02:43,020 --> 00:02:44,370
from verified hardware.

86
00:02:45,180 --> 00:02:46,490
Under the hood:

87
00:02:46,720 --> 00:02:48,630
a sixteen-rule policy engine,

88
00:02:49,020 --> 00:02:50,510
a Rust vault on NEAR,

89
00:02:50,640 --> 00:02:52,330
NEAR Intents for the money,

90
00:02:52,180 --> 00:02:54,430
and NEAR AI for the words.

91
00:02:55,980 --> 00:02:58,490
On eighteen thousand replayed positions,

92
00:02:58,940 --> 00:03:00,750
thirty-four percent were liquidated

93
00:03:00,600 --> 00:03:01,710
without protection.

94
00:03:02,060 --> 00:03:03,070
With Lifeline,

95
00:03:02,920 --> 00:03:04,310
twenty point six.

96
00:03:05,860 --> 00:03:07,250
Even in a harsher test,

97
00:03:07,420 --> 00:03:09,710
where every crash lands within one minute,

98
00:03:09,980 --> 00:03:11,290
liquidations still fell,

99
00:03:11,140 --> 00:03:14,330
to twenty-nine point one percent.

100
00:03:14,180 --> 00:03:17,810
Fifteen hundred and nineteen TypeScript

101
00:03:17,660 --> 00:03:20,810
tests and sixty-two contract tests

102
00:03:20,660 --> 00:03:22,530
run on every change.

103
00:03:23,840 --> 00:03:24,990
Three in the morning.

104
00:03:25,300 --> 00:03:26,130
You're asleep.

105
00:03:26,540 --> 00:03:28,210
And your position is still open.

